<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Convenae</h1><p class="st-meta">72 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.) · capital Lugdunum Convenarum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Mixed community gathered by Pompey in the central Pyrenees, whose town became Saint-Bertrand-de-Comminges.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Their name means those who came together. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerome">Jerome</a>, around 72 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>, returning from his war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-sertorius">Sertorius</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>, settled defeated fighters and mountain people at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lugdunum-convenarum">Lugdunum</a> in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a> valley.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The community mixed Iberian, Aquitanian and Roman elements and quickly adopted Roman ways. Its town had a forum, temple, baths and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Their land was absorbed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-aquitania">Roman Aquitania</a>; Caesar's legate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Crassus</a> campaigned in the region in 56 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lugdunum-convenarum">Lugdunum Convenarum</a> became Saint-Bertrand-de-Comminges, with its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanesque-architecture">Romanesque</a> cathedral, and the region kept the name <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-comminges">Comminges</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 72 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:58.27%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>72 BCE – 56 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lugdunum Convenarum</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aquitanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-64&amp;focus=convenae" aria-label="Convenae on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4694 650 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Convenae lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5014 906L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5014 906h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5014 906h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lugdunum Convenarum. <a href="/atlas?year=-64&amp;focus=convenae">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

